{
  "_comment": "Consumable definitions for the item-drops + crafting lane. Loaded by DeNelle.Village.Items.ConsumableCatalog via DeNelle.Core.CanonicalJson. A consumable's 'id' is also its VillageInventory larder key AND the output id of the matching crafting recipe in consumable-recipes.json - so crafting 'cons_mending_salve' deposits 'cons_mending_salve', and ConsumableUseService.TryUse('cons_mending_salve') consumes it + applies its effect. iconPath -> Resources/ItemIcons/<id> sprite (ItemIconImporter); resolves to null + glyph fallback until art is sliced. WO Consumable-Crafting-V1 added the 8 cons_* roster.",
  "_schemaNotes": {
    "kind": "potion | tent | food. Drives where it can be used and its UI bucket.",
    "effect": "heal | mana | buff | rest. v1 ConsumableUseService implements 'heal' (and 'rest' as a heal); mana/buff/duration (move-speed, spell-power, damage-reduction, AoE damage, blind/slow, ward, all-stats) are DEFERRED - stored as content now, wired to a buff/effect system later.",
    "magnitude": "heal amount (HP) for heal/rest; percent or flat for buffs (deferred).",
    "duration": "seconds for timed buffs/HoT/food (deferred); 0 = instant.",
    "usableInFight": "true = potions/food usable mid-fight; false = rest-only (tent kits).",
    "iconPath": "Resources sprite path (ItemIcons/<id>); glyph is the ASCII fallback."
  },
